From 4402c23c219faf961612017fa5403bb3241bee95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:22:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] world: a seed-independent guard, so every development
 seed can run as itself

check_world_counts required section 3.1's row exactly. That row records SEED 0's
draw, so the guard refused every other seed: seeds 1-5 could only be run by
replacing the function in-process, and every one of their results had to be
labelled DIAGNOSTIC-guard-bypass. The guard was protecting the seed, not the
world.

Measured, dev seeds 0-5 at 200 users: users, patterns_real, gold_discoverable,
decoys and entities are identical on every seed (the generator derives them from
target_users and its own constants). teams, records, gold_rare and sites are
drawn: 12,411-13,131 records, 35-40 teams, 11-21 rare, 7-8 sites.

So the invariant counts are still required to equal the row exactly, and the
drawn ones are held to the structure the benchmark needs instead:
at least the two sites its admission rule compares, a team per site, at least
one record per user, and no more rare patterns than planted ones. Each follows
from the benchmark's definition, not from a band fitted to seeds 0-5.

The table check is kept as table_row_diff(), reported and never enforced: the
run's report carries table_row_diff and the log says what the draw did, so a
run on seed != 0 is self-describing rather than refused. Seed 0 still matches
section 3.1 exactly, and a world that misses a seed-invariant count is still
refused.

What this no longer catches is a record total off by one. That was never a
safety property; it is a draw, and the diagnostic still reports it.

Also repaired, both broken by the archived patch series not carrying their
documentation half (they failed before this change, on the re-applied patches
alone):

- E2E-INGEST.md M13 narrated the pre-re-pin spike hash while report.py carried
  0e05bc00...; the brief now records all four deliberate re-pins. The value is
  verified, not asserted: run.spike_code_hash() computes
  0e05bc00d1cf28ea80ec8e027391585f8312cdd5d84583d63d4fd5860fbeccc8 over 142
  files on this tree, which is what c7 checks.
- E2ESiteProcess.__init__ carried an inline comment the parent's line does not,
  so "replaces step 5 only" failed on a comment. The comment moved to the class
  docstring; the child's step 4 is now the parent's line for line.

Suite floor raised 157 -> 159 deliberately (two tests added).

tests/e2e_ingest: 140 passed / 3 failed before, 143 passed after; the 16
remaining errors are the Live* tests, which need a real nats-server binary that
this container does not have.

